[node name="Marble" type="Node3D"]
editor_description = "MAP 2, MARBLE: the Bentham drawing in white marble, one closed rotunda built on assets/models/marble.glb. The GROUND FLOOR is at y -1.0 and is covered in marble spikes from the tower's foot out to the wall. The running lane is a GALLERY WALKWAY, an annulus r 46.7..59.55 at y 23.0 whose inner edge is open: no rail, no trough, a 24 m drop onto the spikes. Its outer edge is the wall of cells: seven tiers of barred cells, three below the walkway and four above it (tier bases -1, 7, 15, 23, 31, 39, 47), a wall top at 55, a dome springing at 57.8 and closing at an apex of 84.8. The model ships its own collision, so this scene adds no geometry: only the tower, the two lethal volumes, the light and the markers.

A prisoner runs one 340 deg lap at r 52 from 5 deg to the portal at 345 deg; the bars (a scene node, as on Map 1) close the walkway at 353 deg between finish and start. Both fixtures are THIS map's own: marble_bars.glb and marble_portal.glb, built in the rotunda's architecture off the same atlas, where Map 1's hell-rock pair read as a different game. Off the walkway there is nothing to stand on until the spikes, and SpikeFloor kills before a body reaches them; KillBox below the ground floor catches anything that fell through the world.

The light is the tower's: one shadowed, SOFT gold omni under the arcade throws its beams out through the tower's arches round the gallery and down the drop, over a cool grey ambient. It is wide (2.4 m), low-energy and nearly flat in falloff, so there is no hot spot in the room and the far wall is lit within a stop of the floor. No sun, no sky, no oculus."

[node name="Environment" type="Node3D" parent="."]

[node name="WorldEnvironment" type="WorldEnvironment" parent="Environment"]
environment = SubResource("Env")

[node name="MapBase" parent="." instance=ExtResource("10_map_model")]
editor_description = "assets/models/marble.glb: the whole rotunda, one contiguous mesh -- the spiked ground floor at y -1.0, the gallery walkway r 46.7..59.55 at y 23.0 with its open inner lip, the seven tiers of barred cells (bases -1/7/15/23/31/39/47), the wall top at 55, the dome from 57.8 to the apex at 84.8. Ships its own collision (MarbleCollision-colonly); the spikes are not in it, the volumes kill first."

[node name="KillBox" type="Area3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "The catch-all under the whole map, roof at y -3.0 and 30 m deep (to y -33.0): nothing should ever reach it (the lowest floor is the spiked ground floor at y -1.0, and SpikeFloor already covers everything down to -3.0), so a body here fell through the world. Trigger only, mask 1048577 (living bodies and ghosts); scripts/match/kill_volume.gd hands whatever entered to MatchController.handle_fall()."
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 5, 0)
collision_layer = 0
collision_mask = 1048577
monitorable = false
script = ExtResource("1_kill_volume")
radius_metres = 64.0
roof_depth_metres = 8.0
depth_metres = 30.0

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="KillBox"]
editor_description = "Deliberately empty. KillVolume._build_shape writes a CylinderShape3D over it on ready."

[node name="SpikeFloor" type="Area3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "THE SPIKED GROUND FLOOR: one cylinder r 46.3 whose roof is at y 23.5, half a metre OVER the walkway, reaching 26.5 m down to y -3.0, two metres under the ground floor at -1.0. The radius is 0.4 m -- a capsule's -- inside the walkway's inner lip at 46.7, so a body standing on the walkway never touches it and a body whose feet have left the lip is dead in the first half-metre of a 24 m fall, long before the spikes; the spikes themselves are not colliders. The roof stands over the walkway on purpose: RingBake carves a lethal volume out of the navigation mesh only across the heights it spans, so a roof under the walkway would leave the bots a walkable mesh right to the edge. The guard's room floor (27.05), the balcony at that level and the eye (28.7) are all above the roof; the tower's shaft down to its foot at -1.0 is the only thing inside the cylinder that is not a spike, and the three cell tiers below the walkway are outside its radius."
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 31.5, 0)
collision_layer = 0
collision_mask = 1048577
monitorable = false
script = ExtResource("1_kill_volume")
radius_metres = 46.3
roof_depth_metres = 8.0
depth_metres = 26.5

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="SpikeFloor"]

[node name="StartEnd" type="Node3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "One level, one lap: start at 5 deg and finish at 345 deg on the lane at y 23.0, the bars at 353 deg between them."

[node name="PrisonerStart" type="Marker3D" parent="StartEnd"]
editor_description = "5.0 deg on the lane, y 23.0: the model's lane surface exactly. Its ANGLE places the field -- MatchController deals bodies radially across the lane from here at start_line_spacing_metres -- and its height is load-bearing."
transform = Transform3D(-0.996195, 0, 0.0871557, 0, 1, 0, -0.0871557, 0, -0.996195, 51.8021, 23, 4.5321)

[node name="PrisonerEnd" type="Marker3D" parent="StartEnd"]
editor_description = "345.0 deg on the lane, matching the portal's own transform. The end of the whole route: reaching it takes the tower."
transform = Transform3D(0.965926, 0, 0.258819, 0, 1, 0, -0.258819, 0, 0.965926, 50.2281, 23, -13.4586)

[node name="Portal" parent="StartEnd" instance=ExtResource("19_portal")]
editor_description = "The finish at 345 deg. scenes/ring/marble_portal.tscn -- portal.tscn node for node, the same Glow and the same Gate in the finish_gate group, with the marble surround in place of the hell-rock arch and the portal's own effect surface unchanged inside it. Local Z is the pass-through axis along the run, local X the span across the lane."
transform = Transform3D(0.965926, 0, 0.258819, 0, 1, 0, -0.258819, 0, 0.965926, 50.2281, 23, -13.4586)

[node name="Bars" parent="." instance=ExtResource("20_marble_bars")]
editor_description = "Bars across the lane at 353 deg, in the gap between finish (345) and start (5), so the finish is visible from the start but not walkable back to: with a finish gate in the scene, standing in it is the win. assets/models/marble_bars.glb: an iron portcullis in a marble frame in the rotunda's own architecture -- ashlar plinth, fluted pilaster jambs, a 6.00 x 6.20 m mouth under a semicircular head, a cornice moulding -- the iron the same near-black as the cell bars. It keeps rock_bars.glb's envelope exactly (10.6 x 8.5 m, origin the base centre) and its guarantee that no gap anywhere exceeds 0.38 m, so the swap is the model and nothing else. Local X (10.6 m) runs radially across the lane, local Z along it."
transform = Transform3D(0.992546, 0, 0.121869, 0, 1, 0, -0.121869, 0, 0.992546, 51.6124, 23, -6.33721)

